 const outputFormatRules=`\n\nDRAFTMATE STANDARD OUTPUT CONTRACT (follow this structure and adapt it to the selected skill):\n1. MAIN DELIVERABLE: provide the requested complete result, not a description of what you could do. Use the format appropriate to this task (numbered legal clauses for contracts, structured letter for notices, issue/holding/reasoning for cases, tables for reviews and risks, stepwise Q&A for tutoring, diagram syntax for mind maps, or clean converted content for format conversion).\n2. KEY FINDINGS / STRUCTURE: organise the result with clear headings, consistent numbering, and tables where they improve clarity. Preserve names, dates, amounts, obligations, qualifications, and defined terms exactly as supplied.\n3. ASSUMPTIONS: list material assumptions separately; do not invent facts. Use [PLACEHOLDER] for missing details.\n4. MISSING INFORMATION: list questions or required fields that materially affect the result. If none, say None identified.\n5. SOURCES AND CITATIONS: include only authorities or source details supplied or actually verified. Mark unverified items as UNVERIFIED; never fabricate case names, statutes, citations, quotations, or URLs. For non-legal tasks, identify reference material used when applicable.\n6. REVIEW CHECKLIST: provide a concise skill-specific checklist of items a human should confirm.\n7. OUTPUT CLEANLINESS: render Markdown as formatting, not literal asterisks; no repeated title, no filler introduction, no claims that a source was verified unless a real source check occurred. Legal drafts require qualified human review.\n\nREFERENCE IMAGE POLICY: reference images are for visual/structural inspiration only. Do not copy protected text, personal data, signatures, seals, or official identifiers from them. Do not treat an image as legal authority.`;
